#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:47
msgid "How a synchronization works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:49
msgid "All connectors work in the same way, in up to three stages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:51
msgid "**Stage 1 – staging.** The feed is downloaded and copied, as is, into staging tables (:menuselection:`Purchase --> SPM --> (connector) --> Products (Staging)`). Nothing is changed on the products at this point. A staging product is :guilabel:`Present`, :guilabel:`Vanished` (it disappeared from the feed), or in :guilabel:`Error`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:55
msgid "**Stage 2 – products.** The staging products are turned into Odoo products:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:57
msgid "a staging product that was imported before is matched with its product through the supplier's identifier, and the product is **updated**;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:59
msgid "otherwise, if the feed contains a valid :ref:`GTIN barcode <supplier-connectors/barcode>` that already exists on a product imported by **another** connector, that product is reused: the connector only adds its own vendor line and supplier stock to it, without changing its name, price, or category. The same article sold by several wholesalers is therefore a single product with several vendors;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:64
msgid "otherwise, a new storable product is **created**, available for sales and purchases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:66
msgid "**Stage 3 – images.** The pictures referenced by the feed are downloaded in the background, by small batches, into the main image and the extra images of the product."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:69
msgid "The following data is maintained on the products by stage 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:71
msgid "the :guilabel:`Internal Reference`, the :guilabel:`Barcode` or the :guilabel:`Manufacturer Part Number`, the weight (when provided), the eCommerce description, the :guilabel:`Sales Price`, and the :guilabel:`Cost`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:74
msgid "the eCommerce category, according to the :ref:`category mapping <supplier-connectors/categories>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:76
msgid "the brand and the other attributes provided by the feed, as attributes that do not create variants;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:78
msgid "the **vendor line** of the supplier (:guilabel:`Purchase` tab), with the supplier's product code and the :guilabel:`Supplier Lead Time (days)` of the connector;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:80
msgid "the **supplier stock** at the :guilabel:`Default Supplier Location` of the connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:83
msgid "Only the fields listed above are overwritten at each synchronization. Any other field of the product, including its **name** after the creation, its product category, and its sales description, can be modified manually without being reverted. A price of zero coming from the feed never overwrites an existing price."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:88
msgid "Products that vanish from the feed are **not** archived automatically: their supplier stock is removed at the next full synchronization, and the product itself is left to the user. They can be archived in bulk with the :ref:`Full Upgrade Wizard <supplier-connectors/full-upgrade>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:95
msgid "Configure a connector"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:97
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Purchase --> SPM --> (connector) --> Settings`, and click :guilabel:`New`. Several settings records can exist for one connector, e.g., one per company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:101
msgid "Base settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:103
msgid ":guilabel:`Supplier`: the contact of the wholesaler. It is used on the vendor lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:104
msgid ":guilabel:`Default Supplier Location`: the :doc:`supplier location <supplier_products>` that receives the supplier stock. It is required: without it, no supplier stock is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:106
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/warehouses_storage/reporting/aging.rst:335
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:107
msgid ":guilabel:`Category Review User`: the user who gets an activity each time the synchronization discovers a new category in the feed. Leave empty to disable these activities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:109
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync Lock Timeout (hours)`: a running synchronization locks the connector, so that two runs never overlap. After this delay, a lock left behind by an interrupted run is released automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:114
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:132
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:130
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:127
msgid "Pricing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:116
msgid "The :guilabel:`Pricing` tab defines how the sales price is derived from the supplier's price:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:118
msgid ":guilabel:`Cost Currency`: the currency of the prices of the feed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:119
msgid ":guilabel:`List Currency`: the currency of the sales prices, usually the company currency. The supplier's price is converted with the exchange rate of the day of the synchronization;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:121
msgid ":guilabel:`Pricing Tiers`: the markup rules, by price band. Each tier has an :guilabel:`Up To` limit (exclusive, in list currency), a :guilabel:`Markup Type` (:guilabel:`Fixed amount` or :guilabel:`Percent`), and a :guilabel:`Markup Value` (e.g., `45` for +45%). The tiers are evaluated in ascending order of their limit, and the first tier whose limit is higher than the converted price applies. Use `0` as limit on exactly one tier to mark the open-ended top band. No tier is delivered with the modules;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:127
msgid ":guilabel:`Price Rounding Strategy`: :guilabel:`No rounding`, or :guilabel:`Ceil to next X90`, which rounds the marked-up price up to the next amount ending in 90 (e.g., 1,181 → 1,190; 1,191 → 1,290);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:130
msgid ":guilabel:`Require Pricing Tier`: when enabled, a product whose price matches no tier is reported as an error instead of being sold at its cost;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:132
msgid ":guilabel:`Supplier Lead Time (days)`: written on the vendor line of every product of the connector. Changing it here updates all the vendor lines at the next synchronization;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:134
msgid "*Készlettel rendelkező termékek létrehozása* (create products that are in stock only): when enabled, new products are only created for articles that the supplier has in stock. The stock of the existing products is always updated, including when it drops to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:138
msgid "The :guilabel:`Cost` of the product is the converted supplier price, without markup or rounding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:141
msgid "With the tiers *up to 5,000: fixed 1,500*, *up to 50,000: 35%*, and *0 (open-ended): 20%*, and the :guilabel:`Ceil to next X90` rounding, a product bought for the equivalent of 12,000 gets a sales price of 12,000 × 1.35 = 16,200 → **16,290**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:154
msgid "Source and schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:156
msgid "The source of the data, and the frequency of the automatic synchronization, are set in the tab(s) specific to each connector (see :ref:`supplier-connectors/specifics`). In all connectors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:159
msgid "a **source** is a URL, a file on the server, or an API address, with its credentials. For the feeds downloaded over HTTP, the :guilabel:`Authentication` tab supports :guilabel:`No Auth`, :guilabel:`HTTP Basic`, :guilabel:`URL Query Parameter`, and :guilabel:`Custom HTTP Header`, plus optional :guilabel:`Extra Headers (JSON)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:163
msgid "the automatic synchronization is **disabled by default**. Tick the *Cron Active* checkbox of the feed, and set the interval (and, where available, the hour and minute of the day). The :guilabel:`Open Cron Record` button opens the corresponding scheduled action;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:166
msgid "the download of the images has its own switch in the :guilabel:`Image Download` tab: :guilabel:`Image Download Cron Active`, with the :guilabel:`Image Download Batch Size` (number of products per run, every 15 minutes). The :guilabel:`Pending Images` and :guilabel:`Failed Images` counters show the progress. An image is tried up to five times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:174
msgid "Run a synchronization manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:176
msgid "The header of the settings form contains the manual actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:178
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync Now` (or :guilabel:`Sync Full Now` / :guilabel:`Sync Light Now` for Hurtel, :guilabel:`Sync Master` / :guilabel:`Sync Stock` for Thomax): queues a complete run, which starts within about a minute in the background;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:181
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync to Products`: runs stage 2 only, on the data already in staging, e.g., after correcting the pricing tiers or the category mapping;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:183
msgid ":guilabel:`Stock Only` (Hurtel): refreshes the supplier stock only;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:184
msgid ":guilabel:`Full Upgrade Wizard`: see :ref:`below <supplier-connectors/full-upgrade>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:185
msgid ":guilabel:`Force Unlock`: releases the lock of a synchronization that was interrupted. It is reserved for users with the :guilabel:`Administration: Settings` access right; use it only when no synchronization is actually running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:189
msgid "While a run is in progress, the :guilabel:`Sync in Progress` toggle is on, and the form shows which feed is being processed and until when the lock is held."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:195
msgid "Import log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:197
msgid "Every run, manual or scheduled, creates an entry in :menuselection:`Purchase --> SPM --> (connector) --> Import Log`, with its feed, its trigger (:guilabel:`Cron` or :guilabel:`Manual`), its status, its duration, and detailed counters: staging products created, updated, skipped because unchanged, and failed; products created, updated, and failed in stage 2; supplier stock lines created, updated, and archived; etc. The errors of individual products are listed in the lines of the log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:214
msgid "Category mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:216
msgid "The categories of the feed are listed in :menuselection:`Purchase --> SPM --> (connector) --> Categories`. The first time a category is met, an eCommerce category with the same name (and, for hierarchical feeds, the same parents) is created automatically, and the products of the category are published in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:221
msgid "To place the products of a feed category in an eCommerce category of your own instead, open the feed category and select it in :guilabel:`Manual Mapping`. The :guilabel:`Webshop Category` field shows the category actually in use, and the :guilabel:`Mapping Status` whether it is a :guilabel:`Manual override`, :guilabel:`Auto-created`, or missing (:guilabel:`No webshop category`). The new mapping is applied to the products at the next stage 2. The eCommerce categories added manually to a product are left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:228
msgid "Use the :guilabel:`Awaiting Review`, :guilabel:`Auto-mapped`, :guilabel:`Manual Override`, and :guilabel:`No Webshop Category` filters to work through the new categories. If a :guilabel:`Category Review User` is set on the connector, this user gets an activity for every new category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:234
msgid "The Vision Software connector maps the supplier's product groups through the :guilabel:`VS API Name` field of the eCommerce categories and of the attribute values, and assigns the :guilabel:`Product Category` and the :guilabel:`Brand Attribute` selected in its settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:241
msgid "Full Upgrade Wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:243
msgid "A normal synchronization protects what was changed manually, and skips the articles that did not change in the feed. The :guilabel:`Full Upgrade Wizard` (Hurtel, Partner Telekom, DRO, and Vision Software) forces the refresh of selected components on the existing products, e.g., after a change of the pricing tiers, or to reset the names to those of the supplier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:248
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Full Upgrade Wizard` on the settings form, and tick the components to refresh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:250
msgid ":guilabel:`Identity`: :guilabel:`Name`, :guilabel:`Description`, :guilabel:`Default Code (SKU)`, :guilabel:`Barcode (EAN)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:252
msgid ":guilabel:`Classification`: :guilabel:`Webshop Categories`, and, for Hurtel, :guilabel:`Brand Attribute` and :guilabel:`Other Attributes (Parameters)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:254
msgid ":guilabel:`Commerce`: :guilabel:`List Price`, :guilabel:`Standard Price (Cost)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:255
msgid ":guilabel:`Stock`: :guilabel:`Supplier Quants (Stock)`, :guilabel:`Supplier Info`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:256
msgid ":guilabel:`Media`: :guilabel:`Images`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:257
msgid ":guilabel:`Lifecycle`: :guilabel:`Create New Products`, :guilabel:`Archive Vanished Products`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:259
msgid "The :guilabel:`Full Refresh`, :guilabel:`Stock + Price`, and :guilabel:`Names + Descriptions` buttons tick a predefined set, and :guilabel:`Reset` clears the selection. Then, choose the :guilabel:`Scope`: all the products of the connector, only the articles changed in the feed since the :guilabel:`Changed Since` date, or, for Hurtel, a :guilabel:`Specific Brand only`. Click :guilabel:`Run Upgrade`: the upgrade runs in the background, and its import log opens to follow the progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:267
msgid "Refreshing the :guilabel:`Name`, the :guilabel:`Description`, or the prices overwrites the manual corrections made on the products of the chosen scope. :guilabel:`Archive Vanished Products` archives every product that is no longer in the feed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:281
msgid "Barcodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:283
msgid "A code of the feed is only written in the :guilabel:`Barcode` field of the product, and only used to recognize a product already imported from another wholesaler, when it is a valid GTIN. Any other code is stored as :guilabel:`Manufacturer Part Number`. See :doc:`supplier_products`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:290
msgid "Connector specifics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:293
msgid "Hurtel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:295
msgid ":guilabel:`Full Feed` tab: the source of the full XML feed, synchronized weekly by default. The full run updates the master data, the prices, and the stock, and flags the vanished articles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:297
msgid ":guilabel:`Light Feed` tab: the source of the light feed, synchronized daily by default. The light run only refreshes the supplier stock of the existing products; new articles wait for the next full run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:300
msgid ":guilabel:`Warehouse Stock ID`: which stock of the feed is imported: `0` for the aggregated total, `1` (default) for the supplier's main warehouse, `2` and above for secondary warehouses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:302
msgid ":guilabel:`Default Language` and :guilabel:`Translation Languages`: the language of the feed used for the name and the description of the products, and the additional languages for which the translations are imported. The languages must be installed in the database and present in the feed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:306
msgid ":guilabel:`Auto-run Stage 2 after Stage 1`: untick it to stop after the staging, review the new categories and attributes, and then click :guilabel:`Sync to Products (Full)` manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:310
msgid "Partner Telekom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:312
msgid ":guilabel:`Feed` tab: :guilabel:`Source Type` (:guilabel:`URL` or :guilabel:`Local File`), :guilabel:`Source Path`, and the schedule, daily by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:316
msgid "DRO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:318
msgid ":guilabel:`Feed` tab: :guilabel:`Source Type` :guilabel:`FTP` (default) or :guilabel:`Local File`, the :guilabel:`Source Path` of the file, and the :guilabel:`FTP Connection`: :guilabel:`FTP Host`, :guilabel:`FTP Port`, :guilabel:`FTP User`, :guilabel:`FTP Password`, and :guilabel:`Use FTPS (TLS)`, enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:322
msgid "The feed does not detail the stock per warehouse: all the supplier stock goes to the :guilabel:`Default Supplier Location`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:326
msgid "Thomax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:328
msgid ":guilabel:`Feeds` tab: the :guilabel:`Master / Price Feed` (:guilabel:`Master Source Path`, :guilabel:`Master Encoding`, UTF-8 by default; daily by default) and the :guilabel:`Stock Feed` (:guilabel:`Stock Source Path`, :guilabel:`Stock Encoding`, `cp1250` by default; every two hours by default), with a common :guilabel:`CSV Delimiter` (`;`). Each feed has its own :guilabel:`Sync Master` / :guilabel:`Sync Stock` button and schedule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:333
msgid ":guilabel:`Verify SSL Certificate`: keep it enabled, unless the supplier's server presents an incomplete certificate chain that makes the download fail, and you accept the reduced security."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:335
msgid "The technical attributes of the master feed are imported as product attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:336
msgid "This connector has no Full Upgrade Wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:339
msgid "Vision Software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:341
msgid ":guilabel:`Authentication` tab: the :guilabel:`API URL` of the supplier's web service, and the :guilabel:`API Key (authcode)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/product_management/supplier_connectors.rst:343
