#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:121
msgid "The :guilabel:`Is web` field (:guilabel:`Visible on foxpost.hu` or :guilabel:`Not visible on foxpost.hu`) is meant to control whether the parcel is flagged as visible on foxpost.hu when it is registered. In the current version, every parcel is registered as visible regardless of this setting, so keep the default :guilabel:`Visible on foxpost.hu`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:127
msgid "The recipient phone number is mandatory for every Foxpost shipment: the mobile number is used when set, the landline otherwise, and validating a delivery for a contact without any phone number fails with a blocking message. Foxpost uses it to notify the customer about the parcel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:134
msgid "The :guilabel:`Pricing` tab supports two pricing strategies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:136
msgid "**Fixed price**: when no pricing rule is defined, the shipping price is the sales price of the method's :guilabel:`Delivery Product`, resolved through the order's pricelist. The :guilabel:`Fixed Price` field edits that product's base sales price, and pricelist rules on the delivery product override it per pricelist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:140
msgid "**Banded rules**: adding one or more :guilabel:`Pricing Rules` switches the method to banded pricing by weight, volume, weight × volume, price, or quantity. Rules are evaluated in sequence order and the **first** matching rule wins. When no rule matches (for example, the cart is heavier than the largest weight band), the method stays visible at checkout but is greyed out and cannot be selected — the message *Not available for current order* is shown in place of the price."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:147
msgid "Prices defined in the company currency are converted to the order's pricelist currency automatically, and the standard :guilabel:`Free if order amount is above` option works on top of either strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:152
msgid "Two rules — *weight ≤ 2 kg → 990 Ft* and *weight ≤ 5 kg → 1 990 Ft* — charge 990 Ft for a 1.5 kg cart and 1 990 Ft for a 4 kg cart. A 10 kg cart matches neither band, so the Foxpost method is greyed out and cannot be selected for that cart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:159
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:155
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:151
msgid "Cash on delivery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:161
msgid "The module ships a payment provider named :guilabel:`FoxPost COD, with credit card at parcelmachine or at delivery`, letting the customer pay in cash or by card when picking up the parcel. Like every payment provider, it installs disabled: enable and publish it under :menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> eCommerce: Payment Providers` to offer it at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:166
msgid "The provider only appears on the payment step when a published Foxpost shipping method serves the website and the cart contains physical goods, and its :guilabel:`Maximum Amount` is preset to `150000` — the connector does not support COD parcels above 150 000 HUF — so larger orders never see the option. The same ceiling is enforced a second time at shipping: generating a label whose COD amount exceeds the cap is blocked with the message *\"Maximum cash on delivery amount is 150.000,- HUF\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:173
msgid "After a COD order is placed, the customer sees the confirmation message *\"Your order has been confirmed. Please pay upon delivery.\"* instead of wire-transfer instructions. This is customer-facing copy only: the pending COD payment does not confirm the sales order — confirming it (and creating the delivery) remains a back-office step. The amount to collect is computed dynamically per outgoing delivery (transfer) when the shipping label is generated — one amount covers the whole delivery, with partial shipments, service lines and down payments taken into account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:182
msgid "How the per-delivery COD amount is computed, and the optional fraud screening of COD customers: :doc:`../cash_on_delivery`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:184
msgid "How payment methods are filtered per shipping method, and the COD checkout and confirmation experience: :doc:`../delivery_payment`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:188
msgid "Both preinstalled Foxpost methods list **only** the FoxPost COD provider in their :guilabel:`Enabled payment acquirers` whitelist. Out of the box, a customer choosing Foxpost can therefore *only* pay on delivery — as long as no other carrier's COD provider is enabled, since COD providers are validated on their own track (see :doc:`../delivery_payment`). Add the shop's card and wire-transfer providers to each Foxpost method's :guilabel:`Payment Providers` tab to offer them as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:196
msgid "Website checkout: choosing a parcel machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:198
msgid "When the customer selects a Foxpost parcel machine method on the delivery step of the website checkout, a full-screen window titled *Válasszon Foxpost csomagpontot* opens with the official Foxpost *apt-finder* map — the same searchable map and list customers know from foxpost.hu. Choosing a machine closes the window, saves the machine on the order, and displays the choice under the selected delivery method as *Választott csomagpont:* followed by the machine's name. Clicking the Foxpost method again reopens the map, so the customer can change their pick any time before placing the order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:206
msgid "If the shipping method restricts :guilabel:`Countries`, the chosen machine is validated against that list: a parcel machine located in a country the method does not serve is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:210
msgid "Closing the map without choosing a machine does **not** block the checkout — the customer can still place the order. The missing parcel machine is caught later, when the warehouse validates the delivery: validation is refused with the message *\"Please select a Foxpost parcel machine (APM ID) on the sales order or transfer before validating the delivery.\"*, and staff can pick the machine on the order or transfer at that point (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:217
msgid "The map window texts are currently displayed in Hungarian regardless of the website language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:219
msgid "When the selected carrier is a Foxpost parcel machine method, both the sales order form and the transfer form show a :guilabel:`Foxpost parcel machine` field with a :guilabel:`Select on map` button. The button opens the :guilabel:`Select Foxpost parcel machine` dialog with the same Foxpost map used at checkout; alternatively, the machine's operator ID (e.g. `hu472`) can be typed in directly. The order and all of its transfers share one parcel machine — editing it on the transfer updates the order, and it can only be set on transfers linked to a sales order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:226
msgid "Once the first shipping label has been generated for the order, the field and the button become read-only on both forms: changing the destination machine after the parcel exists in Foxpost's system requires contacting Foxpost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:231
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:222
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:256
msgid "Shipping labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:233
msgid "When an outgoing delivery with a Foxpost shipping method is validated, Odoo registers the parcel with Foxpost and immediately downloads its label:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:236
msgid "The returned parcel identifier is stored on the transfer as :guilabel:`Foxpost parcel ID` and becomes the transfer's :guilabel:`Tracking Reference`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:238
msgid "The PDF label is attached to the transfer and posted to its chatter as `LabelFoxpost-<parcel id>.pdf`, ready to print."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:240
msgid "If Foxpost rejects the parcel (invalid machine ID, malformed data, etc.), the validation stops with a readable error message and nothing is registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:243
msgid "Parcel registration on validation requires the method's :guilabel:`Integration Level` to be :guilabel:`Get Rate and Create Shipment` and the :guilabel:`Generate Shipping Labels` option to be enabled on the operation type (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Operations Types`); both are the defaults for delivery operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:248
msgid "If the label download fails (a network hiccup after a successful registration, for example), the parcel stays registered and the label can be re-downloaded at any time with the :guilabel:`Get Foxpost Label` header button on the transfer. The button is available whenever the transfer already has a parcel ID; labels are printed in A6 size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:254
msgid "Each transfer travels as a single Foxpost parcel with a fixed, medium parcel size — package dimensions and weights are not transmitted to Foxpost. Ship one Foxpost transfer per physical parcel, and make sure the goods physically fit a medium locker compartment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:259
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:252
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:289
msgid "Tracking and statuses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:261
msgid "Once a parcel is registered, the transfer displays its live Foxpost status: :guilabel:`Parcel state` (a human-readable description) and :guilabel:`Parcel state code` (the Foxpost status code). The date of the last status event is also recorded on the transfer, where it drives the delivered-date tracking described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:266
msgid "A scheduled action, :guilabel:`Picking: Update foxpost tracking information`, polls the Foxpost tracking API every 3 hours for every transfer whose parcel has not yet reached a final state (delivered, returned, or expired), so open parcels keep updating without any manual work. The interval can be changed under :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Automation: Scheduled Actions`, and the :guilabel:`Update Foxpost Status` header button on the transfer refreshes a single parcel on demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:273
msgid "When Foxpost reports that the customer has received the parcel — picked it up at the machine, or accepted the home delivery — the event date is recorded on the transfer as the actual customer receipt date. That date feeds the order's delivery status and the delivery-date reporting described in :doc:`../delivery_status_and_dates`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:281
msgid "Summary checklist for a working Foxpost setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:283
msgid "Install the **Delivery Foxpost** module (``eyssen_delivery_foxpost``); the shared delivery, payment, and delivery-status layers install automatically as dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:285
msgid "Get :ref:`test and production API credentials <inventory/shipping_receiving/foxpost-account>` from Foxpost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:287
msgid "In :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Delivery Methods`, open *Foxpost Parcelmachine* and/or *Foxpost Home delivery* (or create new methods with :guilabel:`Provider` set to :guilabel:`Foxpost`), then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:291
msgid "enter the :guilabel:`API User`, :guilabel:`API Password`, and :guilabel:`API Key`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:292
msgid "check the :guilabel:`Delivery type` and, if needed, the :guilabel:`Countries` restriction;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:293
msgid "configure the :guilabel:`Pricing` tab (fixed price or banded rules);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:294
msgid "test in :guilabel:`Test Environment`, then switch to :guilabel:`Production Environment` with the production credentials;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:296
msgid "publish the method so it appears on the website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:298
msgid "To offer COD, enable and publish the :guilabel:`FoxPost COD, with credit card at parcelmachine or at delivery` payment provider under :menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> eCommerce: Payment Providers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:301
msgid "Add the shop's other payment providers (card, wire transfer) to each Foxpost method's :guilabel:`Payment Providers` tab, so COD is not the only choice (see :doc:`../delivery_payment`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:304
msgid "Verify that the outgoing operation type has :guilabel:`Generate Shipping Labels` enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:309
msgid "The customer checks out on the website and selects a Foxpost method. For a parcel machine method, the Foxpost map opens and they pick their machine; for home delivery, the parcel goes to their shipping address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:312
msgid "On the payment step they pay online, or — for orders up to 150 000 HUF — choose *FoxPost COD* and pay at pickup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:314
msgid "The sales order is confirmed — automatically for online payments; for COD orders, confirming it remains a back-office step — and the warehouse processes the delivery. If the customer skipped the machine selection, staff pick one with :guilabel:`Select on map` (or type the ID) on the order or transfer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:318
msgid "Validating the transfer registers the parcel with Foxpost, stores the :guilabel:`Foxpost parcel ID`, and attaches the printable label to the chatter. For COD orders, the amount to collect for this specific delivery is computed and sent along (see :doc:`../cash_on_delivery`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:321
msgid "The tracking cron keeps the :guilabel:`Parcel state` up to date. When the customer receives the parcel, the receipt date is recorded and the order's delivery status updates accordingly (see :doc:`../delivery_status_and_dates`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:328
msgid "``eyssen_delivery_foxpost`` — the Foxpost carrier connector: the *Foxpost* shipping provider with parcel machine (APM) and home delivery modes, the map-based parcel machine picker (checkout and backend), banded/fixed pricing, parcel registration and PDF labels, tracking synchronization, and the *FoxPost COD* payment provider record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/foxpost.rst:333
msgid "The connector builds on shared eYssen modules documented on their own pages: the per-carrier payment filtering and COD checkout experience (:doc:`../delivery_payment`), the dynamic per-delivery COD amount (:doc:`../cash_on_delivery`), and the delivered-date tracking (:doc:`../delivery_status_and_dates`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:5
msgid "GLS integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:7
msgid "*GLS* is one of the most widely used parcel carriers in Hungary, offering both home delivery and pickup at a nationwide network of *parcel shops* (the GLS flavour of pickup points). The eYssen GLS integration connects Odoo to the *MyGLS* API so a webshop can offer both delivery modes, let the shopper choose a parcel shop on the official GLS map at checkout, print shipping labels straight from delivery transfers, follow every parcel through the GLS tracking states, collect cash on delivery (COD), and even turn parcels that bounce back to the sender into return orders (RMAs) automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:15
msgid "The feature is delivered by the ``eyssen_delivery_gls`` module, with two optional extensions: ``rma_delivery_gls`` for return automation and ``eyssen_stock_multi_warehouse_delivery_gls`` for warehouse-to-warehouse shipments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:29
msgid "The integration talks to the GLS *MyGLS* system, so a MyGLS business contract is required. GLS provides the following, which are entered on the shipping method in Odoo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:32
msgid "a **client number** identifying the contract;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:33
msgid "an **API user** and **API password** for the production system;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:34
msgid "a separate **test API user** and **test API password** for the GLS test environment (the shipping method form requires all credential fields to be filled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:37
msgid "Request the test credentials as well when onboarding: they allow label generation and tracking to be tried end to end against the separate GLS test system before going live."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:41
msgid "Odoo never transmits the MyGLS password in clear text — every API call authenticates with a SHA-512 digest of the password, as required by the MyGLS API convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:47
msgid "Installing ``eyssen_delivery_gls`` creates two ready-made shipping methods, :guilabel:`GLS Parcel Shop` and :guilabel:`GLS Home delivery`. To configure them (or to create additional GLS methods), go to :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Delivery Methods` and open the method. With :guilabel:`Provider` set to :guilabel:`GLS`, two extra tabs appear on the form: :guilabel:`Pricing` and :guilabel:`GLS Configuration`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:53
msgid "For the generic fields shared by all carriers — :guilabel:`Delivery Product`, availability countries, publishing the method on the website — refer to :doc:`third_party_shipper`. Remember to **publish** each method that should be offered in the webshop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:68
msgid "On the :guilabel:`GLS Configuration` tab, fill in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:70
msgid ":guilabel:`API User` and :guilabel:`API Password`: the production MyGLS credentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:71
msgid ":guilabel:`Test API User` and :guilabel:`Test API Password`: the credentials for the GLS test system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:73
msgid ":guilabel:`Client number`: the MyGLS client number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:75
msgid "The standard :guilabel:`Environment` toggle of the shipping method decides everything at once: in the *Test* environment, Odoo calls the GLS test API with the test credential pair; in the *Production* environment, it calls the live API with the production pair. No other switch is needed when going live."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:81
msgid "The credential fields are only visible to users with :guilabel:`Administration / Settings` access. If the applicable credentials are left empty, validating a GLS delivery does **not** fail: the transfer is validated normally and a chatter note records that no GLS parcel was created, so an unconfigured method never blocks the warehouse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:89
msgid "The :guilabel:`Delivery type` field on the :guilabel:`GLS Configuration` tab selects how the parcel reaches the customer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:96
msgid "Topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:97
msgid ":guilabel:`Parcel Shop` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:99
msgid "Where the parcel goes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:100
msgid "A GLS parcel shop chosen by the shopper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:101
msgid "The customer's own address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:102
msgid "Checkout behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:103
msgid "The GLS map opens to pick a shop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:104
msgid "Behaves like any normal carrier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:105
msgid "Shipping address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:106
msgid "Optionally replaced by an auto-created parcel-shop address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:107
msgid "The customer's delivery address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:108
msgid "Label requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:109
msgid "A parcel shop must be selected before a label can be generated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:110
msgid "No extra requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:112
msgid "For parcel-shop methods, the extra option :guilabel:`Create Delivery Address for PS` controls what happens to the order's shipping address once a shop is chosen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:115
msgid "**Enabled**: a separate delivery address named after the shop (its name and identifier) is created under the customer, carrying the shop's street, ZIP, city and country, and it becomes the order's shipping address. Auto-created shop addresses are hidden from the checkout address chooser and cleaned up automatically when they are no longer used by any order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:119
msgid "**Disabled** (default): the shipping address stays the customer's own; only the parcel shop identifier is stored on the order and sent to GLS with the label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:132
msgid "The :guilabel:`Pricing` tab offers two pricing modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:134
msgid "**Banded pricing**: add one or more rows to the :guilabel:`Pricing Rules` list. Each rule matches on the order's weight, volume, price or quantity; the rules are evaluated in sequence and the **first matching rule** sets the shipping price (converted to the order's currency when the company currency differs). If no rule matches — for example, the cart is heavier than the last band — the method remains listed at checkout but cannot be selected: Odoo shows *Not available for current order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:140
msgid "**Fixed price**: when no pricing rule is defined, the shipping price is the sales price of the method's :guilabel:`Delivery Product`, resolved through the order's pricelist; the :guilabel:`Fixed Price` field edits that product's base sales price, and pricelist rules on the delivery product override it per pricelist (and therefore per website)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:146
msgid "Two rules — *weight <= 2 kg → 990 Ft* and *weight <= 10 kg → 1 590 Ft* — charge 990 Ft for a 1.5 kg cart and 1 590 Ft for a 7 kg cart, and show the GLS method as *Not available for current order* for a 25 kg cart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:150
msgid "The core carrier option :guilabel:`Free if order amount is above` keeps working on top of both modes: when it applies, the shipping price drops to zero while the real cost is still recorded on the order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:157
msgid "Installing the module also creates the GLS-specific :guilabel:`Payment on Delivery` payment provider — a COD-style provider that lets the shopper place the order online and pay the courier or the parcel shop at handover; the sales order itself is still confirmed in the back office (see :doc:`../delivery_payment`). It is created disabled, like any payment provider, and must be enabled and published before use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:163
msgid "Both shipped GLS methods pre-list this provider as the only entry of their :guilabel:`Enabled payment acquirers` list, so out of the box a GLS delivery offers *only* COD at the payment step — as long as no other carrier's COD provider is enabled: the whitelist reliably restricts online providers, while COD providers are validated on their own track (shipping-address compatibility). Add the shop's card or wire-transfer providers to each method to offer more. How the per-carrier payment filtering and the COD checkout experience work is described in :doc:`../delivery_payment`; how the exact amount to collect for each shipment is computed (partial shipments, down payments, order-total cap) is described in :doc:`../cash_on_delivery`. To hold back deliveries until payment is actually received, see :doc:`../payment_gated_delivery`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:174
msgid "The :guilabel:`Payment on Delivery` option only appears at checkout when at least one GLS method is published on the website and the cart contains physical products."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:178
msgid "FlexDeliveryService and options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:180
msgid ":guilabel:`FlexDeliveryService`: when enabled, parcels are announced to GLS with the recipient's e-mail address, so GLS notifies the customer about the delivery and lets them interact with it (GLS *FDS* service). The :guilabel:`FDS Countries` list restricts the service to selected destination countries; leave it empty to apply it everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:184
msgid "A :guilabel:`GLS Box` package type (carrier :guilabel:`GLS`) is shipped under :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Package Types`, ready to be used when packing GLS parcels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:189
msgid "Website checkout: choosing a parcel shop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:191
msgid "When the shopper selects a GLS parcel-shop method at checkout, the **official GLS map** opens automatically in a dialog: it shows every GLS parcel shop in Hungary with its own search and map controls. After the shopper picks a shop, the dialog closes and the selection is stored on the order. Depending on :guilabel:`Create Delivery Address for PS`, the shipping address is either switched to the auto-created shop address or left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:197
msgid "Switching to another delivery method reverts the shipping address to the customer's own address and removes the now-unused shop address; selecting a different shop replaces the previous one the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:209
msgid "Choosing a shop is **not enforced** at checkout: a shopper can close the map without picking one and still place the order. The safety net is at fulfilment time — generating the label for such an order stops with the message *\"Please select a GLS parcel shop on the sales order or transfer before validating the delivery.\"*, and staff fill in the missing shop before shipping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:214
msgid "Back-office users can view and change the chosen shop as well: on the sales order (and on the linked transfer), a :guilabel:`GLS parcel shop` field appears next to the delivery address for parcel-shop methods, together with a :guilabel:`Select on map` button that opens the same GLS map inside the backend. The identifier can also be typed manually (for example `HU-123456`). The field locks as soon as a label exists or the order is done or cancelled, so the shop can no longer diverge from what is printed on the label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:224
msgid "Labels are generated from the outgoing transfer, either automatically through the standard carrier flow when the transfer is validated, or manually with the :guilabel:`Print GLS Label` button on the transfer form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:228
msgid "One GLS shipment is registered per transfer. The :guilabel:`GLS parcel count` equals the number of packages on the transfer (or 1 when the goods are not packed), so multi-package transfers should use :guilabel:`Put in Pack` once per physical parcel *before* printing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:231
msgid "GLS requires complete contact data: the company's phone number and e-mail, and the recipient's phone number and e-mail must all be set, otherwise label generation stops with an explicit message naming what is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:234
msgid "On success, the transfer stores the :guilabel:`GLS parcel ID` and the :guilabel:`GLS parcel number` (one number per package, comma-separated), the label PDF is saved in the :guilabel:`GLS label` field and attached to the chatter named after the parcel number, and each package on the transfer receives its own parcel number — the packages list gains :guilabel:`GLS parcel number` and :guilabel:`Parcel state` columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:239
msgid "When the order was placed with :guilabel:`Payment on Delivery`, the amount to collect is computed for the outgoing transfer at label time and sent to GLS together with the label request — one amount covers all packages of the transfer (see :doc:`../cash_on_delivery`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:244
msgid "**Re-printing creates a new parcel.** The :guilabel:`Print GLS Label` button disappears once a label exists, because clicking it again does not re-download the existing label — it clears the stored parcel data and registers a **brand-new parcel** with GLS, while the previously created parcel stays live in the GLS system (there is no cancellation call). A second, always-visible copy of the button is available in developer mode for deliberate regeneration; use it only when the original parcel is really not going to be shipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:254
msgid "The module ships a catalogue of 90 GLS parcel states, editable under :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> GLS Parcel States` (visible to administrators). Each state has a code, a translatable name, and a :guilabel:`Delivered State` checkbox; the two \"parcel has been delivered\" states (codes `05` and `92`) come pre-flagged as delivered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:259
msgid "Tracking is synchronised automatically by two scheduled actions that run every three hours: one polls every in-flight labelled transfer, the other rotates through labelled packages (a limited batch per run, each package at most once per hour by default). The latest status text, the mapped state and the status date are stored on the transfer and on the matching package. Users can also refresh on demand with the :guilabel:`Update GLS Status` button in the transfer header, or the inline :guilabel:`Update` arrow next to the :guilabel:`Parcel state`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:266
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:309
msgid "Two automations build on the state catalogue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:268
msgid "**Auto-validation**: on the operation type (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Operations Types`), tick :guilabel:`Validate Picking on Delivery` and pick the states in :guilabel:`Validate on GLS States`. A transfer is then validated automatically as soon as its parcel — or, for packed transfers, **all** of its packages — reaches one of the chosen states. Packed transfers are validated without creating a backorder; an unpacked transfer is only auto-validated when it can be validated outright (a partial unpacked transfer is left open for manual processing). This suits flows where the transfer is kept open until GLS confirms the handover or the delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:276
msgid "**Delivered date**: when a parcel reaches a state flagged :guilabel:`Delivered State`, the date the customer actually received the goods is stamped on the transfer. This feeds the delivery status and dates shown on sales orders and the customer portal — see :doc:`../delivery_status_and_dates`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:282
msgid "The raw status text returned by GLS is in Hungarian regardless of the user's language; the mapped state name from the catalogue is translatable and is the one to rely on in multilingual databases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:287
msgid "Returns: automatic RMA on return-to-sender"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:289
msgid "The optional ``rma_delivery_gls`` module automates the return side of GLS shipping. It is **not** installed automatically together with the other modules — auto-creating return orders has financial consequences, so an administrator must install it deliberately per database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:294
msgid "Automatic RMA when a parcel bounces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:296
msgid "GLS reports parcels that the customer never picked up with the state \"The parcel has been returned to sender.\" (codes `23` and `40`). The module pre-flags these two states in its data; the flag is a technical field on the state record and is not shown in the :guilabel:`GLS Parcel States` list — adjust it in developer mode if a different state set is needed. The module also extends the tracking cron to keep polling recently shipped parcels *after* the transfer is done, until they reach a delivered or returned state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:303
msgid "When an outgoing customer delivery reaches a flagged state, **one** auto-approved, return-only :abbr:`RMA (Return Merchandise Authorization)` is created on its sales order, covering all delivered returnable lines, and the order is flagged as needing a refund. The automation is best-effort and safe: a failure never breaks the tracking update — it is logged and escalated as a to-do activity (:guilabel:`Automatic non-pickup RMA failed`) on the salesperson, and the next status update retries cleanly. Repeated status updates never create duplicate RMAs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:311
msgid "GLS return labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:313
msgid "For an approved return RMA, the module generates a GLS **return label**: the customer's address is the pickup side and the company's address the destination. The RMA's :guilabel:`Return Method` selects the GLS return service:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:321
msgid ":guilabel:`Return Method`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:322
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:323
msgid ":guilabel:`Parcel Locker`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:324
msgid "The customer drops the parcel in a GLS locker; when GLS issues a locker PIN for the parcel, it is stored as :guilabel:`GLS Locker PIN` next to the label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:326
#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:100
msgid ":guilabel:`Parcel Shop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:327
msgid "The customer hands the parcel in at any GLS parcel shop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:328
msgid ":guilabel:`Collect from Customer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:329
msgid "A GLS courier collects the parcel at the customer's address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:331
msgid "The result is stored on the RMA's :guilabel:`GLS Return` tab: the :guilabel:`GLS Return Parcel` number, the :guilabel:`GLS Locker PIN` (locker returns, when GLS issues one), the downloadable :guilabel:`GLS Return Label` PDF and the :guilabel:`GLS Return Status`. A return label is generated automatically when a customer-initiated (webshop portal) B2C return is approved; for RMAs created in the backend, RMA managers generate the label with the :guilabel:`Generate GLS Return Label` button. Once a return parcel exists, re-generation is skipped, so no duplicate parcels are registered. Searching RMAs by a scanned return parcel number finds the record directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:340
msgid ":doc:`Withdrawal declarations <../../../../sales/withdrawal>` are excluded — they are handled manually, and no GLS return label can be generated for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:343
msgid "A daily scheduled action, :guilabel:`GLS: Update Return Parcel Tracking`, follows the return parcels until they reach a delivered state, updating the :guilabel:`GLS Return Status` on each RMA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:350
msgid "The optional ``eyssen_stock_multi_warehouse_delivery_gls`` module adapts the GLS carrier to the eYssen multi-warehouse internal-transfer flow, for companies that ship goods **between their own warehouses** with GLS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:354
msgid "Labels printed for a transfer step of an internal transfer are addressed warehouse-to-warehouse: the source warehouse is the sender and the destination warehouse the recipient (each shown as the company name together with the warehouse address), instead of company-to-customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:357
msgid "When a transfer chain recreates the packages for its next step, the GLS parcel identity (parcel ID and parcel number) is copied along, so tracking follows the physical parcel across the legs of the transfer — including intercompany legs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:360
msgid "The internal transfers list can be searched by GLS parcel number through its :guilabel:`Tracking Number` search field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:363
msgid "Install this bridge only when both the multi-warehouse module and the GLS carrier are in use; it has no configuration of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:369
msgid "A complete GLS rollout touches the following settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:371
msgid "**Modules**: install ``eyssen_delivery_gls``; add ``rma_delivery_gls`` (return automation — a deliberate, per-database decision) and ``eyssen_stock_multi_warehouse_delivery_gls`` (warehouse-to-warehouse shipping) only where needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:374
msgid "**Shipping methods** (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Delivery Methods`): on :guilabel:`GLS Parcel Shop` and :guilabel:`GLS Home delivery`, fill the :guilabel:`GLS Configuration` tab (credentials, :guilabel:`Client number`, :guilabel:`Delivery type`, :guilabel:`Create Delivery Address for PS`, :guilabel:`FlexDeliveryService`), set the :guilabel:`Environment`, configure the :guilabel:`Pricing` tab, and publish the methods on the website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:380
msgid "**Payments**: enable and publish the :guilabel:`Payment on Delivery` provider; review each GLS method's :guilabel:`Enabled payment acquirers` list and add the shop's other providers (see :doc:`../delivery_payment`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:383
msgid "**Operation types** (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Operations Types`): optionally enable :guilabel:`Validate Picking on Delivery` and select the :guilabel:`Validate on GLS States` for the outgoing operation type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:386
msgid "**State catalogue** (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> GLS Parcel States`): review the :guilabel:`Delivered State` flags (codes `05` and `92` by default). With ``rma_delivery_gls``, the non-pickup RMA trigger flags (codes `23` and `40` by default) are technical fields on the state records, not shown in the list — adjust them in developer mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:390
msgid "**Scheduled actions**: the transfer- and package-tracking crons run every three hours; the return-tracking cron (with ``rma_delivery_gls``) runs daily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/gls.rst:392
msgid "**System parameters** (:menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> System Parameters`) tune the polling volume. None of these parameters exists by default — the built-in default applies until the parameter is created manually with a different value:"
