#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:5
msgid "MPL integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:7
msgid "**MPL** is the parcel service of Magyar Posta, the Hungarian postal operator. The ``eyssen_delivery_mpl`` module connects an Odoo webshop and warehouse directly to the MPL API v2: customers choose between home delivery and pickup at an MPL *parcel point* (Csomagautomata, PostaPont or Postán maradó) during checkout, the warehouse prints A6 PDF shipping labels straight from the delivery order, tracking statuses are synchronized automatically against MPL's tracking-event catalogue, and a dedicated *MPL COD* cash on delivery (COD) payment method transmits the amount to collect with every label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:25
msgid "MPL shipping requires a business contract with Magyar Posta and access to the **MPL API v2**. The integration authenticates with OAuth2 client credentials, so the following values must be obtained from Magyar Posta before configuring Odoo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:29
msgid "a *Client ID* / *Client Secret* pair for the **test** (sandbox) environment;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:30
msgid "a *Client ID* / *Client Secret* pair for the **production** environment;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:31
msgid "the customer accounting code (*Vevőkód*), sent with shipment and parcel-point API requests;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:32
msgid "the eight-character agreement number (*Megállapodásszám*) of the Magyar Posta contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:35
msgid "Start with the test credentials and the :guilabel:`Environment` toggle set to *Test*. The module then talks to Magyar Posta's sandbox, so labels and shipments created while testing never enter the real MPL network. Switch the carrier to *Production* only when the flow has been verified end to end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:45
msgid "Two shipping methods ship preconfigured with the module: :guilabel:`MPL Parcel Shop` (pickup at a parcel point) and :guilabel:`MPL Home delivery`. To review or create one, go to :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Delivery Methods` and set the :guilabel:`Provider` field to :guilabel:`MPL`. Doing so reveals two extra tabs on the form: the :guilabel:`MPL Configuration` tab and a :guilabel:`Pricing` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:51
msgid "For the generic fields shared by every carrier — such as :guilabel:`Delivery Product`, :guilabel:`Countries` availability or the free-over threshold — refer to :doc:`third_party_shipper`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:56
msgid "To generate MPL shipping labels when a delivery order is validated, set the :guilabel:`Integration Level` option to :guilabel:`Get Rate and Create Shipment`. Labels can also be created manually at any time with the :guilabel:`Print MPL Label` button on the transfer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:72
msgid "The fields on the :guilabel:`MPL Configuration` tab are only visible to users with :guilabel:`Administration: Settings` rights:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:75
msgid ":guilabel:`Test Client ID` / :guilabel:`Test Client Secret`: the sandbox credential pair, used while the carrier's :guilabel:`Environment` is set to *Test*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:77
msgid ":guilabel:`Production Client ID` / :guilabel:`Production Client Secret`: the live credential pair, used in *Production*. The secrets are masked on screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:79
msgid ":guilabel:`Accounting Code (Vevőkód)`: the Magyar Posta customer accounting code, transmitted as a header with shipment registrations and parcel-point catalog queries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:81
msgid ":guilabel:`Agreement Number (Megállapodásszám)`: the eight-character contract number, transmitted as the sender's agreement on every shipment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:84
msgid "If a label is created, or a synchronization is triggered manually, without credentials for the active environment, the operation stops with an explicit error message. The scheduled catalog synchronization logs the failure and retries on its next run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:91
msgid "The :guilabel:`Delivery type` field on the :guilabel:`MPL Configuration` tab decides how the carrier behaves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:102
msgid "The customer's delivery address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:103
msgid "An MPL parcel point chosen by the customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:104
msgid "Checkout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:105
msgid "Behaves like any other carrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:106
msgid "Opens the parcel-point selector; the order cannot be confirmed until a point is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:107
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:108
msgid "Registered as a home-delivery shipment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:109
msgid "Registered for pickup at the selected point, using the point's service type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:111
msgid "A parcel point is one of three MPL service point types, all offered together in the selector:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:113
msgid "**Csomagautomata** (parcel locker) — an automated locker, typically available around the clock;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:114
msgid "**Postán maradó** (post office hold) — the parcel is held for collection at a post office;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:115
msgid "**PostaPont** — a staffed pickup location, usually operated by Magyar Posta's retail partners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:117
msgid "The type of the point the customer picks is stored on the sales order together with the point's identifier and name, and is transmitted to MPL when the label is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:120
msgid "The :guilabel:`Create Delivery Address for PS` option (off by default, parcel-point carriers only) makes the webshop create a separate delivery address under the customer for the chosen parcel point and set it as the order's shipping address. When the customer later switches to another delivery method, the shipping address reverts to the customer and the temporary parcel-point address is cleaned up automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:129
msgid "The module-added :guilabel:`Pricing` tab supports two pricing modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:131
msgid "**Banded pricing**: add one or more :guilabel:`Pricing Rules` (by weight, volume, price or quantity). Rules are evaluated in order and the *first* matching rule sets the shipping price; if no rule matches, the method remains listed at checkout but cannot be selected — Odoo shows *Not available for current order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:135
msgid "**Fixed fallback**: when no pricing rule is defined, the shipping price is the sales price of the method's :guilabel:`Delivery Product`, resolved through the order's pricelist; the :guilabel:`Fixed Price` field edits that product's base sales price, and pricelist rules on the delivery product override it per pricelist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:140
msgid "Standard carrier mechanics — the free-over threshold, margins and taxes — are applied on top of both modes, exactly as for any other shipping method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:144
msgid "Selecting *any* MPL method at checkout also adds a :guilabel:`Handling service` product line to the order (default sales price: 2 000 in the company currency — i.e. 2 000 HUF on a Hungarian database — priced through the order's pricelist). The line is removed automatically when the customer switches to a non-MPL method. To disable this surcharge, set the sales price of the *Handling service* product to ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:153
msgid "The module ships a payment provider named :guilabel:`MPL COD, with credit card at parcelshop or at delivery`. Like every provider, it must be enabled and published before it appears at checkout, and it is only offered when the website has a published MPL shipping method and the cart contains physical products."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:158
msgid "The amount to collect is computed per outgoing delivery (transfer) — partial shipments, service lines and invoiced down payments are all handled by the shared computation described in :doc:`../cash_on_delivery`, and the result is stored in the :guilabel:`COD Amount` field of the transfer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:162
msgid "The amount is transmitted as a whole number: orders in HUF are sent as-is; orders in another currency are converted to HUF at the current exchange rate when the label is created, and the order's currency code is transmitted alongside the amount. Verify foreign-currency COD orders with Magyar Posta before relying on this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:166
msgid "The :guilabel:`COD Bank Account` field on the :guilabel:`MPL Configuration` tab is sent as the payout account for collected amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:168
msgid "Which payment methods are offered together with each MPL shipping method — and the COD-specific checkout experience — is controlled by the per-carrier payment filtering described in :doc:`../delivery_payment`. Out of the box, the shipped MPL carriers only allow their own COD provider — as long as no other carrier's COD provider is enabled, since COD providers are validated on their own track (see :doc:`../delivery_payment`) — so add the shop's card or wire-transfer providers to the carriers to offer a choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:176
msgid "When a COD shipment is split into several packages, the current integration transmits the *full* COD amount with every package. Ship COD orders as a single package, or verify with Magyar Posta how multi-package COD dispatches are collected, to avoid over-charging the customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:181
msgid "Phone number validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:183
msgid "MPL requires a valid **Hungarian mobile or phone number** for every shipment. When a label is created, the module takes the delivery address's :guilabel:`Mobile` number, then its :guilabel:`Phone` number, then falls back to the parent contact, and normalizes the result to the international ``+36`` format (numbers entered with the domestic ``06`` prefix are converted automatically). If no number is found, or the number is not Hungarian, label creation stops with a blocking error — the integration is domestic-only in this respect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:193
msgid "Parcel-point catalog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:195
msgid "The webshop selector does not query Magyar Posta on every page view. Instead, the module keeps a **local catalog** of all MPL parcel points (name, address, coordinates and service point type), kept up to date by the daily scheduled action :guilabel:`MPL: Sync Delivery Places`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:199
msgid "the full list of Csomagautomata, Postán maradó and PostaPont locations is downloaded from the MPL API, using the credentials of a configured MPL shipping method;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:201
msgid "existing entries are updated in place, new ones are added, and points that no longer exist at Magyar Posta are removed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:203
msgid "each entry records when it was last synchronized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:205
msgid "An order that already stores a chosen point keeps working even if that point later disappears from the catalog — the point's identifier and name are copied onto the order at selection time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:209
msgid "Right after installation the catalog is empty until the scheduled action first runs. The backend selector helps out in this state: searching by ZIP code or city fetches matching points live from the MPL API and stores them locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:214
msgid "Website checkout: choosing a parcel point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:216
msgid "When a customer selects an MPL parcel-point shipping method at checkout, a full-screen selector opens immediately, and the checkout cannot continue until a point is chosen — a warning is shown under the shipping method until then. The selected point is displayed under the method, stored on the order, and restored automatically when the customer returns to the checkout later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:221
msgid "The selector has two modes, decided by the website configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:228
msgid "Map widget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:229
msgid "Searchable list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:230
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:231
msgid ":guilabel:`Google Maps API Key` set in the website settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:232
msgid "none (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:233
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:234
msgid "Magyar Posta's official *PostaPont* map widget on a Google map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:235
msgid "Built-in list with type filters (Csomagautomata / Postán maradó / PostaPont), text search and paging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:237
msgid "Data source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:238
msgid "Loaded live from Magyar Posta"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:239
msgid "The local :ref:`parcel-point catalog <inventory/shipping_receiving/mpl-catalog>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:240
msgid "Service point type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:241
msgid "Not provided by the widget — shipments are registered with the generic *PostaPont* delivery mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:243
msgid "Stored with the selection and transmitted to MPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:245
msgid "To enable the map mode, go to :menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> Settings`, find the :guilabel:`MPL` block and enter a :guilabel:`Google Maps API Key`. Leave the key empty to use the searchable list, which needs no external service beyond the daily catalog synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:249
msgid "Back-office users can pick or change the point without the webshop: the sales order and the transfer both show an :guilabel:`MPL parcel point` field with a :guilabel:`Select on map` button that opens the :guilabel:`Select MPL parcel point` dialog — a searchable list with :guilabel:`Parcel locker`, :guilabel:`Post office hold` and :guilabel:`PostaPont` filters. The field locks once the shipment has been registered with MPL or the order is done or cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:258
msgid "Labels are generated in **A6 PDF** format, ready for label printers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:260
msgid "With the :guilabel:`Integration Level` set to :guilabel:`Get Rate and Create Shipment`, validating the delivery order registers the shipment with MPL automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:262
msgid "The :guilabel:`Print MPL Label` button on the transfer creates the shipment manually at any time; it disappears once a label exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:264
msgid "On success, the transfer stores the :guilabel:`MPL parcel ID`, the :guilabel:`MPL parcel number` (when the shipment is registered by validating the transfer, the number is also copied to the standard tracking reference; the manual :guilabel:`Print MPL Label` button fills only the MPL fields) and the downloadable :guilabel:`MPL label`, and the label PDF is attached to the transfer's chatter together with the tracking number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:270
msgid "When the products are packed into several packages, one parcel is registered per package, and each package's shipping weight is transmitted individually (weights are sent in grams, with a minimum of 100 g and a default of 1 kg when no weight is set). When MPL returns per-package tracking numbers, each package record stores its own number so parcels can be followed one by one; otherwise, the packages share the shipment's tracking number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:277
msgid ":guilabel:`Print MPL Label` is not a reprint button. Pressing it clears the stored parcel data and registers a **new** shipment with MPL. For this reason it is hidden once a label exists; re-registering a shipment is only offered to users with developer mode enabled. To reprint an existing label, download the stored :guilabel:`MPL label` file or the chatter attachment instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:284
msgid "The sender address transmitted to MPL is always the **company address**, not the warehouse address. Merchants shipping from several warehouses appear towards MPL under the company's registered address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:291
msgid "The module ships MPL's tracking-event catalogue — 46 states across the pickup, processing, transport and delivery phases — as editable records under :menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> MPL Delivery States`, each with a :guilabel:`State Code`, :guilabel:`State Category`, :guilabel:`MPL State Name` and a :guilabel:`Delivered State` checkbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:297
msgid "Statuses are refreshed automatically by two scheduled actions, each running every three hours:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:299
msgid ":guilabel:`Picking: Update MPL tracking information` polls every transfer that has an MPL parcel number and is not yet done or cancelled;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:301
msgid ":guilabel:`Package: Update MPL tracking information` polls individual packages, up to 50 per run, spacing repeat checks of the same package by the configured :guilabel:`Tracking Check Interval` (default: 60 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:305
msgid "The latest state, its code and its timestamp are shown on the transfer (:guilabel:`Parcel state`, :guilabel:`Parcel state code`, :guilabel:`Parcel state date`) and on each package; the transfer also has an :guilabel:`Update MPL Status` button for an on-demand refresh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:311
msgid "**Delivered date**: when a tracking event maps to a state whose :guilabel:`Delivered State` box is checked, the date the customer actually received the goods is stamped on the transfer (the actual customer receipt date), using the delivery timestamp reported by MPL. This feeds the order-level delivery progress described in :doc:`../delivery_status_and_dates`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:315
msgid "**Auto-validation**: on the operation type (:menuselection:`Inventory app --> Configuration --> Operations Types`), the :guilabel:`Validation on MPL Delivery` group offers :guilabel:`Validate Picking on Delivery` together with a :guilabel:`Validate on MPL States` list. Once *every* package of a transfer reaches one of the selected states, the transfer is validated automatically. This enables a deferred-validation flow: leave the delivery order open after printing the label, let the scheduled actions follow the parcel, and have Odoo close the transfer when MPL reports delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:324
msgid "When using the deferred-validation flow, set the shipping method's :guilabel:`Integration Level` to :guilabel:`Get Rate` (or untick :guilabel:`Generate Shipping Labels` on the operation type). With :guilabel:`Get Rate and Create Shipment`, the automatic validation registers the shipment with MPL a *second* time, because the :guilabel:`Print MPL Label` button does not fill the standard tracking reference that suppresses the validation-time registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:331
msgid "None of the 46 shipped states is pre-flagged as delivered. Tick :guilabel:`Delivered State` on the terminal *Kézbesített* (delivered) rows after installation — otherwise neither the delivered-date stamping nor a delivery-based auto-validation setup has any effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:336
msgid "The transfer-level scheduled action deliberately skips transfers that are already done. If deliveries are validated immediately at shipping time, tracking keeps refreshing only through the package-level action and the manual :guilabel:`Update MPL Status` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:343
msgid "Checklist to take MPL live:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:345
msgid "Install ``eyssen_delivery_mpl``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory/shipping_receiving/setup_configuration/mpl.rst:346
